{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>When a man has a wayward and rebellious son.</b> Because of his end he is put to death, as Rashi explained. And if you ask: since he is put to death because he is destined to rob people, he should not be liable to a severe death — for a robber is [punished] by the sword, whereas this one is by stoning! It appears to say: since it is written ״he does not listen to the voice of his father and the voice of his mother,״ it is like one who curses his father and his mother, which is by stoning, as it is said: ״אביו ואמו קלל דמיו בו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:14.140407871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}